 * ============================================================================
 * CEE MOCK PORTAL — all-in-one Google Apps Script web app
 * MBBS/BDS entrance mock-test practice system (Nepal CEE pattern)
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * DEPLOYMENT
 *   1. Create (or open) a Google Sheet — this script stores all data there.
 *   2. Extensions -> Apps Script, delete default code, paste THIS whole file.
 *   3. Save, then Deploy -> New deployment -> type "Web app":
 *        Execute as: Me        Who has access: Anyone
 *   4. Open the web app URL. The Users / Questions / Attempts / Responses tabs
 *      are created automatically (the question bank seeds itself with 8 demo
 *      questions if empty). Teacher account: register, then promote yourself
 *      by changing Role cell "student" -> "teacher" in the Users tab (first
 *      teacher bootstrap) — or edit the row directly.
 *
 * WHAT'S INSIDE
 *   - doGet() serving the embedded single-page frontend (base64 EMBEDDED_HTML)
 *   - Google Sheets data layer (5 tabs incl. Messages, LockService-serialized)
 *   - SHA-256 password hashing, 24h sessions, one-device lock, login rate limit
 *   - Deterministic seeded exam engine: server-side scoring (+1 / −0.25 / 0),
 *     mock + custom practice modes, instant-feedback practice, idempotent
 *     submission, late/auto-submit detection, bank-drift text-match fallback
 *   - Student analytics + leaderboard, teacher class analytics + CSV export,
 *     per-student drill-down, MailApp messaging (quota-aware),
 *     in-app student→teacher messaging with teacher inbox, printable
 *     per-attempt teacher reports
 *   - Question bank CRUD with duplicate protection + bulk upload with
 *     server-side dry-run preview + PDF helper
 *   - MailApp emails: registration, approval/rejection, results, password
 *
 * NOTE: functions ending with "_" are private (not callable via
 * google.script.run). The public surface is the documented API plus the two
 * brief-required utilities hashPassword() and shuffleArray().
 * ============================================================================
 */

